text.section:
The instrument of dedication may:

Contain restrictions and other provisions relating to management, use, development, transfer, and public access, and may contain any other restrictions and provisions as may be necessary or advisable to further the purposes of this article;


Define, consistently with the purposes of this article, the respective rights and duties of the owner and of the Commonwealth and provide procedures to be followed in case of violations of the restrictions;


Recognize and create reversionary rights, transfers upon conditions or with limitations, and gifts over; and


Vary in provisions from one natural area preserve to another in accordance with differences in the characteristics and conditions of the several areas.
